         "2023-03-28T08:44:17.949-07:00\nEileen - Meeting in SF w/ Phil on 3/28/23\n\n\n\nFounders:\n\n-Phil (classmate/friend from GSB)- Has a family business in Germany part of which does home foundations and resi solar so use to dealing with fragmented workforce\n\n\n\nProduct\n\n-automating design for resi heatpump systems\n\n\n\n* Arch (fka 2zero, aka Aurora for heat pumps—Chris and Sam are investors alongside Floodgate, Coatue, and ReGen)\n  * *Background- we did our dual degrees together and I was actually in the same class (Understanding Energy) where he formed the idea for this company. Needed to work for McKinsey for visa reasons after school, but has been working on it for 5 years and was able to get an e-visa when he raised the round. He has a very fun entrepreneurial background which I’ll more about share live on Tuesday.*\n  * Meticulously focused on two things at this stage: Building product and hiring the right people— only hires people that are “smarter than him”, for their last hire he sorted through 175 candidates and when their top choice said no, he went back to drawing board rather than take their second choice! Most of their engineers have at least one exit under their belt with a company they joined at stage A-C. The obsession continues with their investors—had two offers @ 2x the valuation of Coatue, but felt like David was the right person to help scale\n  * Rather than try to do too much, laser focused on nailing their first use case: help HVAC installers create better designs and proposals\n2023-02-28T12:19:46.688-08:00\nAia Sarycheva from Bessemer told me about this",
